<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  EggLayersLayEggs.xml                      Jawa_Patches - new file 2026-08-22
  ============================================================================

  🔴 NINETEEN OF OUR XENOTYPES CARRY A GENE THAT PROMISES EGG-LAYING AND DOES
  NOTHING. They give live birth. The gene is `Outland_EggLayer` (Outland -
  Genetics, neronix17) and its own description reads, verbatim:

      "Carriers of this gene reproduce by laying an egg rather than typical
       pregnancy."

  MEASURED, not suspected, against the live 578-mod dump:
    * `Outland_EggLayer` has `geneClass` **Verse.Gene** - the plain base class,
      which has no behaviour of its own.
    * Its ONLY modExtension is Vanilla Expanded Framework's `GeneExtension`.
      That class serialises 21 fields and the only one touching reproduction is
      `pregnancySpeedFactor`, which the gene sets to **1** - no effect. There is
      no egg field of any kind in it.
    ⇒ nothing anywhere reads this gene. It is a description and an icon.

  🔑 THE PREGNANCY SYSTEM ACTUALLY IN PLAY IS INTIMACY - GENDER WORKS, and it
  drives egg-laying off `SEX_Ovipositor`, whose mod extension names an ovipositor
  as the `femaleReproductiveReplacement`. That mod ALSO replaces vanilla
  `PregnancyUtility.CanEverProduceChild` outright, so it is the only pregnancy
  path that runs.

  ⭐ THIS PATCH IS THE MOD AUTHOR'S OWN PATTERN, not an invention. Intimacy ships
  overlap patches that do exactly this for every foreign egg gene it knows about
  - `Alpha_Genes_egg_overlap.xml`, `VRE_Saurid_egg_overlap.xml`,
  `VRE_Insector_egg_overlap.xml` - swapping them for `SEX_Ovipositor`. It has no
  patch for Outland, because Outland is not a mod it was written against. This
  file is the missing one.

  ⚠️ `Outland_EggLayer` IS DELIBERATELY KEPT beside the new gene rather than
  removed. It carries the icon and the flavour text the species pack chose, and
  its `exclusionTags` (Egglaying · AG_Egglaying · Reproduction) are what stop a
  third egg gene stacking on top. `SEX_Ovipositor` declares no exclusionTags at
  all, so the two cannot conflict.

  🔑 ONE XPATH REACHES ALL NINETEEN, and that is on purpose: the predicate is
  "whichever xenotypes claim to lay eggs", not a list of names that decays the
  moment the species pack is updated. Verified with lxml against
  RimMandrake_StarWarsRaces/Defs/XenotypeDefs/RimMandrakeXenotypes.xml -
  19 matches, which is exactly the count in the live dump.
  ⚠️ It would also reach a future non-RimMandrake xenotype carrying the same
  gene. Measured today, all 19 are ours; if that changes, this is the file to
  narrow.

  ⚠️ TWO GUARDS, AND THEY GUARD DIFFERENT THINGS. `MayRequire` sits on the `<li>`
  because the risk there is the GENE not existing - a xenotype listing a gene no
  mod supplies logs a cross-reference error every load. The surrounding
  `PatchOperationConditional` guards the XENOTYPES not existing: a
  PatchOperationAdd whose xpath matches nothing throws red on every launch, and
  it would match nothing if our own species pack were ever unloaded.

  ⛔ WHAT THIS FILE DOES NOT DECIDE: whether those nineteen SHOULD lay eggs.
  That was settled by whoever put `Outland_EggLayer` on them, and Wookieepedia
  confirms it for only some - Trandoshan, Gungan, Nautolan, Geonosian, Duros and
  Nikto are explicit in the article text; Aqualish, Falleen, Feeorin, Gand and
  Klatoonian are simply silent on reproduction. Changing the ROSTER is a design
  call for the owner. This file only makes the game do what our defs already say.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- Every xenotype that claims to lay eggs now actually does. -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[genes/li="Outland_EggLayer"]/genes</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[genes/li="Outland_EggLayer"]/genes</xpath>
      <value>
        <li MayRequire="LovelyDovey.Sex.WithRosaline">SEX_Ovipositor</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!--
    🔴 THE HUTT IS THE ONE SPECIES ON THE WHOLE 70-XENOTYPE ROSTER THAT
    WOOKIEEPEDIA CALLS HERMAPHRODITIC: "multiple sex organs and utilized
    hermaphroditic reproduction" (Hutt/Legends). It carried no reproductive gene
    at all, so every Hutt was taking the gender default - phallor if male, gestor
    if female - which is the one thing a Hutt canonically is not.

    `SEX_AlwaysAphrodor` gives both organs regardless of gender, so a Hutt can
    play either role. Conception in this load is decided purely by organs and
    never by gender, so this is the whole change; nothing else is needed.

    ⛔ NOT `SEX_Meiosis`, even though Jabba self-impregnating to produce Rotta is
    the canonical precedent. That gene's own effect text says it "prevents
    regular conception", so it would replace Hutt reproduction with selfing
    rather than add to it. If the owner wants the Rotta case it is a deliberate
    second decision, not a free extra.
    ⚠️ The hermaphroditism is LEGENDS. Canon confirms only the brood pouch, which
    nothing here models.
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RSW_RimMandrakeHutt"]/genes</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationAdd">
      <xpath>Defs/XenotypeDef[defName="RSW_RimMandrakeHutt"]/genes</xpath>
      <value>
        <li MayRequire="LovelyDovey.Sex.WithRosaline">SEX_AlwaysAphrodor</li>
      </value>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
